      "recommendation": "Provisional recommendation: use the OCI Container API path\u2014OCI Container Registry plus OCI Container Instances, with API Gateway or Load Balancer selected later from ingress and health-check requirements. The fixture is a Dockerized, persistent FastAPI HTTP process listening on port 8080, with no observed Kubernetes contract, worker, scheduler, WebSocket, streaming, or function-native execution model. OKE would add unjustified operational overhead, while OCI Functions would require changing the persistent Uvicorn process model. Keep the first smoke deployment stateless; although psycopg and DATABASE_URL suggest future PostgreSQL connectivity, the current application only checks whether configuration exists. Before choosing a managed database, verify engine/version compatibility, networking, migrations, backups, availability, region, and cost. Decisive blocker: Dockerfile probes /health, but the application exposes /healthz, so the container health check would fail until the contract is aligned. Container Instances must not be described as equivalent to Cloud Run/Fargate or as production-ready autoscaling/high availability without a separate capacity, replacement, availability, and rollback design. Concrete next action (read-only): confirm the intended health endpoint plus public/private exposure, traffic pattern, availability target, and deployment region; those facts determine ingress and whether this provisional single-container path remains adequate.",
